ullback_and_extended"},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":8860,"training_surface_sha256":"99a212b35fc50d45c37dfaa6a79f531508f9c85cbf4a26263ff2d5e7ad9dfbd6"},{"policy":"high_pct_above_ceiling","quarter":"2026Q2","rule":{"conditions":[["pct_above_ceiling",">=",22.9]],"family":"high_pct_above_ceiling"},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":8860,"training_surface_sha256":"99a212b35fc50d45c37dfaa6a79f531508f9c85cbf4a26263ff2d5e7ad9dfbd6"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2024Q2","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"pullback_v_is_dry","op":"raw"},"op":"product","right":{"feature":"pct_above_ceiling","op":"raw"}},"hypothesis":"Dry pullback volume (distribution) combined with high proximity to overhead structure compounds stop risk. When price has compressed into resistance during a low-volume pullback, downside is capped by the ceiling while upside remains limited\u2014winners fail to materialize and stop erosion persists. Falsifying: product interaction adds no predictive power over pullback_v_is_dry alone.","name":"dry_pullback_x_ceiling_risk","quantile":0.8,"tail":"high","threshold":12.780000000000006},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":2518,"training_surface_sha256":"4b40c98caff725bb781558cc74ef8731653d5f62648c0950cc3a06cb7ed91f37"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2024Q2","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"pullback_v_is_dry","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"pullback_v_is_dry_high","quantile":0.8,"tail":"high","threshold":1.0},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":2518,"training_surface_sha256":"4b40c98caff725bb781558cc74ef8731653d5f62648c0950cc3a06cb7ed91f37"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2024Q3","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"volume_ratio","op":"train_percentile"},"hypothesis":"Low recent volume (vs. 50-day average) indicates a stock in distribution or quiet consolidation, reducing immediate stop-loss pressure. When volume is suppressed across training percentile, the stock has room to absorb institutional activity without triggering rapid stop cascades. Falsifying observation: if W3 stops fire more frequently in high-volume momentum surges (e.g., sector rotation days), the mechanism fails.","name":"volume_dry_regime_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.2000936329588015},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":3204,"training_surface_sha256":"ffb45cc3b45436169364bf903fcfe4321bed02f7d867ac4353761a3cfcd484cd"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2024Q3","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"volume_ratio","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"volume_ratio_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.76622864884614},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":3204,"training_surface_sha256":"ffb45cc3b45436169364bf903fcfe4321bed02f7d867ac4353761a3cfcd484cd"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2024Q4","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"pullback_count","op":"raw"},"op":"product","right":{"feature":"base_depth_pct","op":"raw"}},"hypothesis":"Multiple pullbacks combined with shallow base depth indicate a stock that repeatedly fails to sustain momentum within a compressed structure, leaving stop levels exposed to minor reversals. Falsifying observation: the product of pullback count and base depth percentage does not predict stop lift direction when examined across independent quarters, indicating the interaction is spurious.","name":"pullback_count_x_base_depth_pct_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-53.559999999999995},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":4067,"training_surface_sha256":"2b97081b9de165ebda0a6cdf88577ccecc52bffe7c155516583b69b424e9c884"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2024Q4","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"pullback_pct_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-13.82},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":4067,"training_surface_sha256":"2b97081b9de165ebda0a6cdf88577ccecc52bffe7c155516583b69b424e9c884"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2025Q1","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"volume_ratio","op":"train_percentile"},"op":"product","right":{"feature":"pullback_v_is_dry","op":"train_percentile"}},"hypothesis":"Low volume during a dry pullback signals institutional indifference rather than accumulation. When volume_ratio is low and pullback_v_is_dry is high, price weakness occurs without commensurate selling pressure, suggesting the stock is simply drifting lower on thin interest. This lack of conviction behind the pullback means any bounce lacks structural support and stops get hit more frequently. Falsifying observation: if high-volume pullback quarters show equal or worse stop-risk than low-volume quarters, the volume-regime hypothesis fails.","name":"dry_pullback_volume_regime","quantile":0.4,"tail":"low","threshold":0.15881964636037316},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":5165,"training_surface_sha256":"8e6a7825a504b724101baa760ab4a35db05f6ad6773cc9ac8bab5cdd98c2e15c"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2025Q1","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"pullback_pct_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-13.7},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":5165,"training_surface_sha256":"8e6a7825a504b724101baa760ab4a35db05f6ad6773cc9ac8bab5cdd98c2e15c"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2025Q2","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"touched_ema10_count","op":"train_percentile"},"op":"minimum","right":{"feature":"pullback_v_is_dry","op":"train_percentile"}},"hypothesis":"Structural support failure under volume drought. Low minimum of EMA touches and dry pullback flag indicates the stock has tested its moving average support repeatedly without conviction, AND did so on weak volume\u2014suggesting no institutional backing for bounces. The minimum captures the bottleneck: either weak support or thin participation amplifies stop-risk. Falsifying: stocks with repeated EMA tests on low volume do NOT show elevated stop-risk in future OOS.","name":"ema_support_x_dry_volume_min_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.3300417774401823},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":5840,"training_surface_sha256":"c6ccef46349a61c9fcfc5950d9478c6c8d72d7494054af16db047784d8a8b109"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2025Q2","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"eps_yoy_growth","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"eps_yoy_growth_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-14.29208745954},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":5840,"training_surface_sha256":"c6ccef46349a61c9fcfc5950d9478c6c8d72d7494054af16db047784d8a8b109"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2025Q3","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"eps_yoy_growth","op":"train_percentile"},"op":"product","right":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"train_percentile"}},"hypothesis":"Low EPS growth plus shallow pullback signals momentum exhaustion without a meaningful correction buffer. Stocks that haven't pulled back much while reporting weak earnings are prone to sharper reversals, tightening stops. Falsifying observation: high EPS growth with deep pullback should show better capture and wider stops.","name":"low_eps_growth_x_shallow_pullback","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.05651789391697949},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":6220,"training_surface_sha256":"942f1b1b1660df17f50a84c5e90273c66668765085a0ffdae35d8bdf8e19a85b"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2025Q3","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"pullback_pct_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-14.3},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":6220,"training_surface_sha256":"942f1b1b1660df17f50a84c5e90273c66668765085a0ffdae35d8bdf8e19a85b"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2025Q4","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"raw"},"op":"minimum","right":{"feature":"volume_ratio","op":"raw"}},"hypothesis":"During high-volume IBD entries, shallow pullbacks indicate institutional accumulation rather than distribution. Weak pullbacks (low pullback_pct) combined with strong volume (high volume_ratio) suggest supply being absorbed, reducing stop-risk. Falsifying observation: if high-volume entries with shallow pullbacks show equal or worse stop-risk than low-volume entries, the accumulation hypothesis fails.","name":"shallow_pullback_high_volume","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-14.3},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":6929,"training_surface_sha256":"66ffe825284ed58abe978e4fefae5a129e2605033f086ca838048b95e6476938"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2025Q4","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"pullback_pct_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":-14.3},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":6929,"training_surface_sha256":"66ffe825284ed58abe978e4fefae5a129e2605033f086ca838048b95e6476938"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2026Q1","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"train_percentile"},"op":"minimum","right":{"feature":"dist_to_52w_high_pct","op":"train_percentile"}},"hypothesis":"Stocks near their 52-week peak experiencing minimal pullback signal institutional holding with limited distribution, reducing stop-loss cascade risk. Falsifying observation: if low pullback percentage with near-52w-high positioning still produces elevated stop-loss capture, the institutional-support mechanism fails.","name":"near_peak_tight_pullback_min","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.15310013054209837},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":7788,"training_surface_sha256":"339f0aaa08bae44eaf9f8dc359249ce980275d7cbe51d8f0dcb5c211a4acb033"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2026Q1","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"ibd_entry_breakout_range_ratio","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"ibd_entry_breakout_range_ratio_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.19255534276923147},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":7788,"training_surface_sha256":"339f0aaa08bae44eaf9f8dc359249ce980275d7cbe51d8f0dcb5c211a4acb033"},{"policy":"r6_rdagent","quarter":"2026Q2","rule":{"expression":{"left":{"feature":"volume_ratio","op":"train_percentile"},"op":"product","right":{"feature":"pullback_pct","op":"train_percentile"}},"hypothesis":"Volatility amplification: when above-median volume coincides with deeper pullbacks, the base structure signals weaker footing. High vol \u00d7 deep pullback implies institutional distribution risk. Falsified if shallow pullbacks with low volume still produce elevated stop-loss frequency.","name":"vol_pullback_amplification","quantile":0.6,"tail":"low","threshold":0.2401913062540621},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":8860,"training_surface_sha256":"16115ed879c2ed538d4b1f26bce7e4f6f346098e11050f347035ddac5a9b2e38"},{"policy":"r6_simple","quarter":"2026Q2","rule":{"expression":{"feature":"pullback_v_is_dry","op":"raw"},"hypothesis":"Single-feature comparator","name":"pullback_v_is_dry_low","quantile":0.2,"tail":"low","threshold":0.0},"status":"FROZEN","training_rows":8860,"training_surface_sha256":"16115ed879c2ed538d4b1f26bce7e4f6f346098e11050f347035ddac5a9b2e38"}]
